\section{Prior Work}
Keyword spotting on microcontrollers has converged on small convolutional encoders trained under streaming constraints.
\section{Notation}
Throughout, lowercase bold letters denote acoustic frames and uppercase bold letters denote matrices.

\section{Model Architecture}
Our encoder stacks four depthwise-separable blocks behind a causal front end.
\section{Datasets}
We train on two thousand hours of far-field speech augmented with room simulation.

\section{Metrics}
We report false accepts per hour at a fixed false-reject rate on the held-out stream.
\section{Baseline Systems}
We compare against the open-source streaming baseline with a 200-millisecond latency budget.

